---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About Dr. DuBose · Direct Lifestyle Medicine" active="about">

  <!-- 1 · Introduction -->
  <section class="section" style="padding-block:clamp(56px,8vw,96px)">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="photo-frame">
          <div class="photo" style="aspect-ratio:4/5">
            <img src="/images/dr-dubose.jpg" alt="Dr. Logan DuBose" width="800" height="1000" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <h1 style="font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,44px)">Logan DuBose, M.D.</h1>
          <p style="margin-top:20px">
            I&rsquo;m a doctor and researcher. I practice lifestyle
            medicine and lead research on aging, caregiving, and health
            technology. This practice is one doctor with a small number
            of patients.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · My path -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>Why I practice this way</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            I earned my M.D. at the Texas A&amp;M College of Medicine and
            completed an internal medicine internship at George
            Washington University. Since then I have practiced primary
            care and led NIH-funded research on aging, caregiving, and
            digital health tools.
          </p>
          <p>
            In that work I saw how much it helps when one doctor knows
            the whole picture, explains results, and follows up. I also
            saw how much of what makes people sick comes from daily life.
            So I start there, and I use medicine when it is needed.
          </p>
          <p>
            I keep the panel small and costs low. That keeps the price at
            $99 a month, lets visits last as long as they need to, and
            lets me offer some memberships at a reduced fee or free.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · Training and credentials -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>Training and credentials</h2>
          <p style="margin-top:18px"><a class="quiet" href="/writing">Selected research &rarr;</a><br />
          <a class="quiet" href="/cv">Read my full CV &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="row"><b>M.D.</b><p>Texas A&amp;M College of Medicine</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Internship</b><p>Internal medicine, George Washington University</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Licensure</b><p>Virginia (unrestricted), DEA-registered; Texas licensure [at launch]</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Clinical practice</b><p>Primary care physician, Fredericksburg Christian Health Center</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Focus</b><p>Lifestyle medicine: prevention, nutrition, activity, sleep, stress, and the conditions that follow from them</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Research</b><p>Chief Research Officer, Olera; research lead on NIH-funded studies of aging, caregiving, and health technology</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Expected</b><p>Lifestyle medicine board certification, International Board of Lifestyle Medicine, expected January 2027</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Memberships</b><p>American College of Lifestyle Medicine, member since 2026</p></div>
        <div class="row"><b>Education</b><p>B.S. Biochemistry, The University of Texas at Austin; M.B.A., Texas A&amp;M University</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · How I practice -->
  <section class="section band-warm">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>How I practice</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Evidence first</b>
          <p>I recommend what good evidence supports. When the evidence
          is thin or mixed, I say so.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>I explain my reasoning</b>
          <p>You will know what I recommend and why.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>I say &ldquo;I don&rsquo;t know&rdquo; when I don&rsquo;t</b>
          <p>Then I find out, or I find the person who knows.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Lifestyle first, medicine when it is needed</b>
          <p>I start with what you eat, how you move, how you sleep, and
          your stress. I prescribe and treat when that is the right
          choice, not as a last resort and not by reflex.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>I refer when someone else is the right doctor</b>
          <p>You see them for that part of your care, and I stay
          involved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Your decisions are yours</b>
          <p>I make sure you have the information and time to make
          them.</p>
        </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · Outside the practice -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>Outside the practice</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            I&rsquo;m married to a pediatrician I met in medical school. I
            play jazz, read, and write. My wife and I travel, go to live
            comedy, and get to the beach when we can. I have also served
            on medical mission trips to Belize.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 7 · CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>Start with a free conversation.</h2>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
